# TODO: Unsupported features — prioritized

High priority
- ClassDeclaration
  - Why: Core JS/TS feature, needed for most OOP code.
  - Where: src/ir/, src/lowering/, src/codegen/
  - Next action: Add IR node for class, lowering from SWC class AST, codegen -> Rust struct + impl, runtime prototype handling, add unit tests.

- Functions: async / generator / arrow / closures
  - Why: Async/generators are common; closures require environment capture.
  - Where: src/ir/function.rs, src/lowering/, src/codegen/, src/runtime/
  - Next action: Represent async/generator in IR, lower to appropriate runtime/future/iterator patterns, ensure closure environments are captured and tested.

- Modules / Imports / Exports (ESM)
  - Why: Module resolution and exports are necessary for multi-file projects.
  - Where: src/lowering/, src/codegen/, out/
  - Next action: Implement module graph, support default/named/namespace imports, output modularized Rust or runtime loader, add integration tests.

- Runtime Value model (Object/Array/Function/Promise)
  - Why: Accurate runtime semantics required for correct behavior.
  - Where: src/runtime/
  - Next action: Complete Value type, property lookup/prototype chain, arrays internals, promises scheduling; add tests.

- Error handling: try/catch/finally / throw
  - Why: Control-flow semantics and stack behavior.
  - Where: src/ir/, src/codegen/, src/runtime/
  - Next action: Lower try/catch to error propagation model (anyhow/runtime errors), implement catch binding and finally semantics, add tests.

Medium priority
- TypeScript types: generics / unions / intersections
  - Where: src/lowering/, src/ir/types.rs
  - Next action: Add lightweight IR for generics/union shapes; focus on runtime shape checks needed by codegen.

- Destructuring / Spread / Rest
  - Where: src/lowering/, src/codegen/
  - Next action: Implement lowering patterns that create temps and correct copy/assign semantics.

- Iteration constructs: for..of, for..in, switch
  - Where: src/lowering/, src/codegen/
  - Next action: Map to iterator protocols and property enumeration helpers in runtime.

- Template literals / tagged templates
  - Where: src/lowering/, src/codegen/
  - Next action: Support interpolation and tag function call lowering.

Low priority
- Enums (TS and const enums)
  - Next action: Map to Rust enums or const values; optimize when const.

- Decorators / Metadata
  - Next action: Implement decorator application order and metadata storage in runtime.

- JSX/TSX (optional)
  - Next action: If required, transform to runtime calls or React-compatible output in GUI path.

General recommendations
- Start with ClassDeclaration and Functions (async/generator) — they unblock most real-world code.
- For each feature: add tests under tests/, create small TS examples in tests/fixtures/, and ensure build -> rustc flow still works.
- Mark each implemented feature with a short CHANGELOG entry and add TODO comments linking failing tests to tasks.
